# Next.js & UI

## Structure

- App Router under `src/app/`; shared UI in `src/components/`; utilities in `src/lib/`.
- Colocate route-specific components near their route when they are not reused.
- Use `next/link` and `next/image` for internal links and images.

## Components

- Functional components with typed props (`interface` or `type`).
- Extract reusable logic into hooks in `src/hooks/` when used in 2+ places.
- Use shadcn/ui primitives; extend with Tailwind — avoid one-off CSS files unless necessary.

## Styling

- Tailwind utility classes; use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils` for conditional classes.
- Mobile-first responsive design (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`).
- Accessible contrast, focus states, and semantic HTML (`nav`, `main`, `section`, `article`).

## Performance

- Prefer Server Components for static/marketing content.
- Lazy-load heavy client widgets; optimize images (`sizes`, `priority` only for hero LCP).
- Avoid loading unnecessary client JS on content pages.

## Example CTA pattern

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Clear action + href
<Button asChild>
  <Link href="/contact">Book free consultation</Link>
</Button>

// ❌ DON'T: Vague or non-actionable
<Button>Click here</Button>
```
